From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:33:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Name the bus
 of the SPMI slave macOS sleeps"

This reverts commit 8b161049258561f8cb132dec5003ac74726ab003.

With this property in the device tree the boot loader image changes, and
reboots since then stalled in the loader far more often than before (the
loader recovers by itself). Nothing reads the property unless
spmi_sleep_extra is set, and that stays 0. Take it out again to see
whether the stall rate returns to the old one.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index c5a26ba8ca..5eab4b7bfb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -466,12 +466,6 @@ &sio {
 
 /* Deep sleep: the T8132 sleep controller, as the J713 enables it upstream. */
 &sleep {
-	/*
-	 * The J604's macOS sends SLEEP to SPMI slave 8 on nub_spmi_a0 at the
-	 * commit (its S2R record); the J604 has no debug port on SPMI, so the
-	 * bus is named here. Nothing is sent unless spmi_sleep_extra names it.
-	 */
-	apple,spmi-extra-bus = <&nub_spmi_a0>;
 	/*
 	 * The J713's macOS has these at f at the commit; the J604's macOS
 	 * writes none of them before it (q-pwr-s2r-1), DWI stays on under
-- 
2.43.0

